     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. **1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the usual maximum.** Metformin labeling generally caps immediate-release dosing at 2,550 mg/day and extended-release at 2,000 mg/day, even with normal renal and hepatic function. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. For example:\n- **Metformin IR 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin IR 500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **Metformin 1700 mg PO once daily** with an extended-release formulation (1,700 mg/day, within the ER limit)\n- Another dose, if you have a specific indication that supports it\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
